<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21129] TCU: llite trash_can_projid sysfs rejects newline-terminated input ("echo default &gt; ...")</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21129</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;echo default &amp;gt; /sys/fs/lustre/llite/&amp;lt;fs&amp;gt;/trash_can_projid
-bash: echo: write error: Invalid argument
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The store handler compares the buffer with "default" without stripping the trailing newline. It should use sysfs_streq() or strip \n before parsing. Admins and lctl set_param both send newline-terminated values, so the documented "default" keyword cannot be set with echo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Expected"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Expected&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;echo default and echo &amp;lt;number&amp;gt; both work. The MDT-side mdd.*.trash_can_projid store needs the same check, but test_97 did not reach it because the client check failed first.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
